WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:04.350
Even as we speak, the world is 
moving towards destruction.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.230
You must do something quickly.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.170
That's easy for you to say, Flora-chan.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.800
That's just my screen name.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.240
I am the Mysterious Woman.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.480
Fine then, Mysty.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.630
What about Olvidia?

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.370
Why not just use its power?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.240
No.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.340
That place was made with a 
technology lost to us now.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.210
You can't go there.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.290
A lost technology, huh?

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.510
This is my world's highest 
form of technology.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.810
There's something I want to ask 
of you, using these and Alma Gear.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.550
What are you planning to do?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.360
I've got an idea.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.290
Hurry!

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.170
We don't have a second to lose!

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.220
We've got a mission! 
It's to stop this war!

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:42.850
<i>Please.</i>

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.140
<i>You have to make it.</i>

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.680
Kon, we don't have time for this.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.470
Sorry, just gimme a second.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.440
I've got a chronically sedentary 
lifestyle and I'm not good at running.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.080
The war could start any time now!

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.370
Yeah, but I still don't see how running 
over there is going to help anything.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.090
I think finding some sort of 
transportation would get us there quicker.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.960
You're so pathetic.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.720
Says the guy who just has to wait 
around for a shoulder to sit on.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.970
How could you possibly understand 
this crippling pain in my side?!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.720
I wanna ride on someone's shoulder, too!

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.430
Sainglain, I want you to tie Kon's legs 
together with rope and drag him along.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.020
I'm not a log!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.860
Please don't do stuff like that!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.650
I'd be ripped to pieces before 
we even got to the battlefield!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.990
Body and soul!

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.420
Those are...

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.150
They don't look too good.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.620
And what's up with the 
bags under their eyes?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.250
I think they'll have those forever.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.880
They are definitely engaging 
in some unhealthy practices.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.010
What the hell are you?

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.890
I will assume this is the St. Piria 
Empire's 36th princess and her retinue?

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.230
Hey, you!

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.510
How about answering the question 
of who the hell are you?!

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.720
If you keep answering a 
question with a question,

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.820
eventually, you will kill all 
conversation in the universe!

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.530
I am very sorry, but I cannot 
let you go any further.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.180
Please do not get angry with me.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.280
It's no good.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.910
This guy isn't even trying 
to have a conversation.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:36.270
But why do they keep 
going "oooh-aaaah"?

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.000
It's like they're in some 
choir or something!

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.300
They are Ulbrion.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.630
Artificial Hyperion created

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:48.020
with the science and secrets 
of our Ulga Sorority.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.110
Their agility can block out any light,

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.890
and their strike will 
topple the very mountains!

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.640
Ulbrion, you say?

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.450
Couldn't you have worked on them 
and their name a little more?

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.560
'Cause no offense,

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.190
but whatever they're supposed to be, 
it looks like you failed pretty hard.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.380
It seems like they made 
the name by combining

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.620
the "Ul" from the name of their 
sorority, and the "rion" from Hyperion.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.040
I can't make more sense 
of it than that.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.330
All right, but where 
did the "b" come from?

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:19.170
What is the "b" supposed to mean?!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.480
Enough from you.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.570
For the first time, 
he engages us in conversation!

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.930
Though it looks like we've 
kind of hurt his feelings.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.860
I think we've been standing 
around here long enough, though.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.120
Come on, old guy.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.660
Give him what you've got.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.940
My pleasure!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.230
May I ask you to wait one moment?

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:47.820
Is there any reason to go 
"kukuku" before you say that?

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:50.700
Ulbrion!

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.160
Prepare to attack.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.670
I don't even know what 
to start laughing at.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.090
What the...?

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.390
They're different now.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.580
We of the Ulga Sorority

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.140
have been researching Ulbrion 
for a very long time now.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:20.460
If you use drugs to enhance 
the abilities of humans,

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.750
you simply cannot avoid it.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:26.180
Yes, the side effects.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.660
The side effects of the forced 
enhancements are mostly psychological.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.310
There are many reports of them

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.890
easily overwhelming their opponents

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.510
only to fail before finishing them off 
because they were

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.840
wracked by sudden headaches or amnesia.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.870
So we thought about that.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.180
If they're going to crack 
when it matters the most,

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.470
why not just let them hang 
loose when they're not needed?

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:55.400
If they only need to be present when 
it's important, they won't fail.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.600
We decided to use this novel concept

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.950
as a base for our research, 
and the result is what you see here,

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.480
an unbeatable fighting force.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:08.360
The strongest fighting machine 
of all time, the Ulbrion!

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.490
You know what, whatever.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.490
We're in a hurry, so let's 
get this over with.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.370
Attack!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.040
They're pretty good.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.710
But they're still knock-offs!

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:28.840
The real Hyperion's strength...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.970
...is something like this!

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.020
Papipupe Polyperion!

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.140
Something Alma, soar!

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.810
Cool.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.410
Maybe I can get away with 
not doing anything at all.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:02.930
Nabokov-sama, we will be 
ready for battle shortly.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:03.870
I'm glad to hear it.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.050
Our military might is quite a sight.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:08.580
Can we win?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.520
Of course.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.880
Even if we were to engage the enemy, 
there is no way we could lose.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.210
And we have reinforcements 
from the Ulga Sorority.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.900
One could say that our 
victory is assured.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.390
Exactly.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.520
The curtain is rising. My era begins.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:30.340
Over there!

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:33.310
Something... Explosion!

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:46.580
Something isn't right here.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.210
It looks like you finally 
saw our true objective.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:56.890
That's right.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.600
Our mission isn't to eliminate you.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:00.760
Just to delay us.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:01.600
Old guy!

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.260
What?

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.390
These guys are only trying 
to buy some time!

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.310
What?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:10.410
They're only here to keep us from 
getting over to Sarisariñama!

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.030
You've noticed, but it's too late.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:18.940
As long as we keep you, 
the unknown variables, here,

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.870
the war will begin on its own.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.700
And then, the world will fall into 
the hands of the Ulga Sorority,

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.830
into the hands of our archbishop!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.280
What the hell is that?

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.160
You're like some caricature 
of a villain!

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.530
It's like you're in love 
with your own wickedness!

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.830
You had those lines planned out!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.410
But I don't understand.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:37.960
What does the start of the war

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.970
have to do with the Ulga Sorority 
taking over the world?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.920
That's a good question.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.240
Both the empire and 
Jugglaburk are hoping

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.770
to gain control of the 
world through this war.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.300
Most of this world's military 
force has been deployed

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:55.330
to Sarisariñama for 
this decisive battle.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.450
Were these forces to be destroyed,

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.220
neither the empire nor Jugglaburk

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:03.200
would have enough power 
to rule the world.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.400
I see.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.010
So you're saying that everybody

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.710
just can't stop themselves from 
wanting to rule the world.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.380
The gears of history have 
been set in motion!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.470
You do not have the power 
to stop our destiny.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:22.000
I think what he's saying is that we 
can't waste any more time on them.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.430
You're right.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.480
But there are too many of them 
to force our way through.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.390
Damn, reinforcements?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.310
I told you already.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.910
You're not going one step further.

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:48.080
This ain't good!

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.250
It keeps getting worse and worse.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:55.880
We don't have any time to spare!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:10:59.760
Damn it.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.760
It's no good. There's too many of them.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:11.900
ED?!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.410
Damn you, Erecpyle!

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.330
What are you doing here?

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:35.950
We are formally declaring 
that I, Erecpyle Dukakis...

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.840
...and his special operations 
unit, Incognito...

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.410
...after evaluating our sense 
of righteousness and justice,

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.600
have decided to distance ourselves 
from the aims of the Ulga Sorority's

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.350
Archbishop Taulepton and 
henceforth be independent!

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.480
From now on, we follow our own path.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:55.360
We finally got rid of 
our annoying shackles!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.860
That's right.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.490
It's been a while, so we're 
not going to hold back.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.990
We're here to support you, DT!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.490
Erec, you're...

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.900
We'll talk later!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.230
Incognito, attack!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.840
Aim for the head!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.160
Nothing else!

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.170
This is a race against time.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.180
We'll decide this in one blow!

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:25.800
Aye!

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.030
Roar, my Alma Gear!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.660
Calibre!

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.800
It's done.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.310
I'm not saying thanks.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.210
Make...

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.240
"Make no mistake."

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:18.530
"I've no intention of 
becoming your friend."

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:20.790
"It just happened to be that 
we shared a common enemy,"

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.620
is what you wanted to say, right?

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:23.380
How...

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:24.830
How did I know?

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.500
Because the lines someone like you says

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.450
are always the same.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:30.460
This...

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.170
"This isn't the time to argue."

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:35.090
"Let's hurry up and get to the battlefield,"
 is what you wanted to say, right?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.280
We will be stopping this war.

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.930
What do you plan on doing?

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:39.460
We're...

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.760
We're going to put an end to

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:46.270
Saying that our goals are the same 
would not be completely wrong.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.940
So I guess we'll have 
a temporary truce.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:50.700
Don't...

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.540
"Don't forget."

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.930
"Our face-off will still happen

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.130
once this war is over," 
is what you were going to say.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:13:59.230
I know.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:04.230
Then let's go.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.260
To the battlefield, to Sarisariñama!

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:19.230
How do you plan on stopping 
this war, anyway?

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.680
I don't know if I can stop it.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.130
But I've done a little 
preparation for it.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.880
So I guess it's just a gamble.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.680
None of your business.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:46.140
All this time, we've been 
traveling to avoid this war.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.120
We must stop it.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:49.470
No matter what.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.460
Nabokov-sama.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.720
All forces stand ready for battle.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.340
Yes, our time has come!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.440
Send word to all troops!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.060
Attack!

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.660
The world is love and peace!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.200
I'd like to ask you all, what 
can we do for world peace?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.880
To this end, I am speaking 
to all you soldiers.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:52.900
Lay down your arms right now and
 cease all hostile activities at once.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:55.070
The world is love and peace.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:59.260
A man called John said that, 
a long time ago.

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.790
What's this voice?

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:04.300
This is a warning.

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:09.740
Whoever does not heed this warning 
will be purged by a great power.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:13.270
We ask anyone who hears this 
message today to pass it along

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.680
in the next three 
days to anyone who hasn't.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.750
Thank you very much.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:17.640
What's happening?

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:19.500
Who is that?

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:23.520
It's understandable if you 
don't recognize my voice.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.500
So let me explain to you.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.380
We are the chosen warriors 
of Ixion's will.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.380
We are the Hyperion!

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:35.700
That's ridiculous!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.410
They're nothing but common traitors!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.190
Attack them!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.010
Attack!

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:43.580
You fools.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.660
Raising your hand against us and

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:49.480
raising your hand against the mighty 
will of Ixion is one and the same.

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:08.290
I urge you to think about it again.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:11.410
Think about the world 
as love and peace.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.680
Will you obey us or not?

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.950
Is this a joke?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.970
Do you think you can fool me so easily?

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:25.020
If you really are the agents of 
Ixion, then show us a miracle!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.270
As you wish.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:31.170
Behold the power of the Hyperion!

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.480
That is what a person of Ixion 
would say, am I correct?

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:36.920
Mysty, you're up.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:37.980
Got it.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.030
Behold.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:43.780
The power of Hyperion!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.970
What's this sound?

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:02.310
That's...

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.240
I-Impossible...

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.060
O-Olvidia!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.200
It's a miracle!

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:21.700
Does this mean that they 
really are the agents of Ixion?!

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.760
I don't want to do this.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.880
Going against Ixion
means going against a god.

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:38.150
I can't do it.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.830
Run!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.660
Idiots!

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:44.670
Don't mess with me!

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.180
Deserters will be shot!

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.810
Hey! Somebody stop them.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:49.810
Are you listening to me?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.540
Hey!

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:54.410
Hey! You!

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.720
Come back here!

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.030
Curses!

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.710
They're running with their 
tails between their legs!

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:03.690
I can almost see Jugglaburk's 
crying face!

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:05.510
Then this is our chance.

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:07.270
We're going to go all in!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.340
Please wait.

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:09.210
What?

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.170
Our soldiers are also leaving 
the field in droves.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.760
The chain of command has been broken!

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:16.660
What?!

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.380
The soldiers are running away.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.770
Looks like Kon's plan 
was a huge success!

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:35.190
I didn't think it would work this well.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.610
Trust Kon to stop an entire 
war just by mouthing off.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.700
No, I'm pretty surprised 
that it actually worked.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.080
Hey, hey.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:49.080
This isn't a time to 
stand back and watch.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:51.210
You're right.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:54.000
We need to proceed to the 
next step immediately.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.050
What do you plan on doing?

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:58.070
We will capitalize on this confusion

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:00.350
to capture both Jugglaburk 
and the emperor.

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:03.590
We are going to make them 
sign a peace treaty.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.300
We'll use force if necessary.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.680
But that means...

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:11.440
Your Highness?

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.240
I don't care.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:18.440
I agree that that will be the 
quickest way to end this war.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.440
I am greatly obliged.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.140
I'm impressed, Hyperion.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.450
Is that what I'm supposed to say?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.350
We never expected 
them to have such power.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.780
It seems Erec and his 
men are also there.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:38.120
So that means they have turned 
their blades against us.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:43.360
Ecarlate shouldn't have 
arrived there at all.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:45.220
What is happening?

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.930
This means the Ulbrion 
did not function.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.720
Well, that...

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:55.060
The new weapon that was supposed 
to surpass the Hyperion, pathetic!

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.690
Our deepest apologies.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:57.800
That's fine.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:00.450
Even if they brought confusion 
to the battlefield,

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.860
our plans will not change.

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:05.100
Almost all of the military 
forces of the world are here.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.160
And that's what matters.

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:08.480
Isn't that so?

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:09.870
Undoubtedly.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.370
Shall we begin then?

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:21.470
Let us witness the world bow to the 
Ulga Sorority with our own eyes!

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.050
The earth is trembling!

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.100
What is happening?

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.350
What's that?

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.520
A giant?

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:40.820
The last boss?

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:46.320
No, not yet!

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:04.670
This is the archbishop's trump card?

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.440
That's a big...

00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:09.050
It's not big, it's too big!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:30.370
Olvidia's...

00:22:34.050 --> 00:22:39.350
Forezo!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:24.810
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:10.790 --> 00:24:14.380
The Ulga sorority's Archbishop 
Taulepton finally reveals

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:16.700
his true ambition and unleashes 
the ultra giant living weapon Forezo

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:21.480
to crush both Jugglaburk's and 
St. Piria's armies to seize the world.

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:22.520
What will I do?!

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:24.280
What's going to happen to my DT?!

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:30.610
The ace up Ulga Sorority's 
Archbishop Taulepton's sleeve was the

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:30.610
awe-inspiring ultra giant 
living weapon, Forezo...

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:35.620
Fo~ re~

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:35.620
zo~! (Sugita)
